  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new motion kernel: `camcraft_motion::multiaxis::radial_drop::RadialDrop` (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/radial_drop.rs`).\n- It gives the exact ball-centre radius at an (axial station, angle) about a stated rotation axis.\n- It works for any model. The model does not have to be a shape of revolution (for example a helical rotor or a carving).\n- The ball comes in along the radial line from far outside. It stops at its first contact with the mesh.\n- The contact is the largest valid root over the face, edge and vertex patches of each facet, grown by the ball radius.\n- No contact gives `None`. The kernel never makes up a radius.\n- Input that cannot be meant is refused by name: a ball radius that is not positive and finite, an empty mesh, a facet with a corner that is not finite, an axis that is not a direction.\n- Angle zero follows the axis.rs basis law (`rotary_flow_unwrap::basis`). Rotary Flow uses the same frame.\n- A cull keeps queries fast: axial bins about one ball radius wide (4096 at most), then a bounding-sphere test against the ray's line.\n- No operation calls the kernel yet. This PR is the third slice of #2772 (`Refs`, not `Fixes`).\n- `docs/decisions/2772-radial-drop.md` records the choices and what was dropped.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe rotary kinds fit their contact for a turned surface. On a part that is not a shape of revolution, the merged slices keep them locked, which is correct. The next safe step is a contact law that is exact for any mesh, proved alone before an operation uses it.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, in `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/radial_drop_tests.rs` (9 tests):\n\n- `a_face_contact_rests_the_ball_r_off_the_plane`\n- `an_edge_contact_rests_the_ball_on_the_ridge`\n- `a_vertex_contact_rests_the_ball_on_the_tip`\n- `the_screw_rotor_drop_touches_and_never_gouges`: 216 stations on a helical screw rotor. At each station the ball touches (distance = r within 1e-7). 200 centres farther out on each ray do not come nearer than r.\n- `the_kernel_agrees_with_a_brute_force_march`: an independent march and bisection agree within 1e-6.\n- `a_facet_reaches_every_station_within_the_ball_radius`: pins the cull.\n- `a_ray_past_the_part_meets_nothing`\n- `the_radial_is_a_unit_vector_square_to_the_axis`\n- `input_that_cannot_be_meant_is_refused_by_name`\n\nRed before the fix: yes. With the test file and no kernel, the build fails with `error[E0432]: unresolved import super::radial_drop`.\n\nMutation checks. For each check I changed the kernel, ran the pins, and then restored the code:\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| M1 no face candidate | red (face, screw, march) |\n| M2 no edge candidate | red (edge, screw, march) |\n| M3 no vertex candidate | red (vertex, screw) |\n| M4 edge foot not checked against the segment | red (vertex, screw, march) |\n| M5 face foot not checked against the triangle | red (vertex, edge, screw, march) |\n| M6 bounding-sphere cull without `+ r` | red (screw) |\n| M7 radius guard accepts 0 and negative | red (refusals) |\n| M8 axial bins without the `r` padding | red (`a_facet_reaches_every_station_within_the_ball_radius`; the first test set missed this, so I added that pin) |\n\nRestored: 9 of 9 pass.\n\nCommands on the final head:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib radial_drop`: 9 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 41 steps, 0 failed (includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `rotary_verify`, `rotary_parallel_keyway`, `continuous_4axis_part`).\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` (base c16df4e7d): 115 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 26.4 min (app heavy and motion heavy, every target).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. I ran the quick gate with `app suites: example_catalog` and the rotary suites. No `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changed (`git diff --stat upstream/main` shows only the 4 files of this PR).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No operation, post or verify path calls the kernel yet. Wiring Rotary Parallel (and Rotary Offset roughing) to it is the next slice. That slice changes posted G-code.\n- The shank is clear only for a ball nose on the same radial line, with a shank no wider than the ball. A tapered or wider holder is not covered here. The wiring slice must keep the existing holder checks.\n- Not timed on the reporter's 1.15 M-facet STEP mesh.\n- No UI change, so no screenshots.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR touches `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/mod.rs` or the new files.\n\nChangelog: none (an internal kernel with no caller yet; the row comes with the wiring slice)\n\nRefs #2772\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
